A||||12||pHoOl||Flame thrower tail pipes||||1||
Z||000000||pHoOl||07-26-2000||01:30 AM||||Any thoughts on how to do it on a fuel injected engine?  I'd be afraid of melting the body, but thought i'd throw the idea out for all of you curious minds who think about things like this.||||reg||1
Z||000001||1FST2M6||07-26-2000||08:20 AM||||#1 remove the cat.. #2 install switched power additional ignition coil. #3 weld in bung for 2 spark plugs in the outlots of eaxh tail pipe. (one per side) connect the coil to the ignition system so that it will only fire when the cars on or when you have fliped the swith. and  finally #4 GO FULL THROTTLE!    ||||reg||1
Z||000002||pHoOl||07-26-2000||11:59 AM||||is this from experience or just in theory.  btw, what's the likely hood of melting the rear facia?  I'd hate to over heat it||||reg||1
Z||000003||1FST2M6||07-26-2000||12:08 PM||||experiance.. My father and i did that to my old 79 Corvette. ZZ Top did that to their CADzilla, and their Old Eliminator coupe. HotRod magazine covers that about once a year. as for melting the facia.. as long as you don't leave it on for 10 minutes straight you'll be fine... you car did get warm but never affected the polyurethane bumper (off an 82 has a wing)  check your local emissions laws.. taking your cat off may be illegal. you can do it with a cat but not very well.. you'll need the unspend fuel for your "afterburners"<p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 07-26-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||HYPTNOTiSE||07-26-2000||05:49 PM||||my car used to shoot out 18inch flames(longest recorded, usually about 6-12.) Out the right side taillight. It wouldn't go out the left. Don't know why it did, i had no egr, and borla exhuast and a lot of mods. Who knows? Might have been a leaky cold start injector, i used to get pretty bad gas milage too.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||pHoOl||07-27-2000||12:25 AM||||yeah, i'm pretty sure taking the cat converter off is illegal, but oh well, who will know.  =)  ||||reg||1
Z||000006||filthyscarecrow||07-27-2000||01:03 AM||||ok, neither of mine have cats, and my 85GT will shoot little ones (but still visible from 100 yards away) when one lifts off from full throttle and does not disengage the clutch. how do i know? i let my friend wind the piss out of it once so i could see what it sounded like from the outside (very nice) and he went by in third gear at about 70mph and lifted and 2 nice blue flames spewed forth into the world. <BR>  i wouldn't worry about the flames melting the bodywork. they are only there for a short time. if your car is constantly shooting flames i might worry, but i'd worry more about what was wrong with it than i would about the bodywork.<P>------------------<BR>me go fast.||||reg||2
Z||000007||86SE||07-27-2000||02:35 AM||||Hmmm, I have no cat converter.........an extra coil.........and a lot of odd sized wire.........hey, im going to have some flame throwin exhaust!!<P>Just one question, ok 2 questions.  #1, To connect the coil to the ignition system do I just tap into all 4 wires that connect to the coil? #2, then put on a coil wire?<P>------------------<BR>'86 Special Edition,<BR>High-Output V-6 Yellow Fiero||||reg||10
Z||000008||olympic||07-27-2000||04:01 AM||||  Maybe you could add one of those ether injectors from diesel trucks and tractors and plumb it in just before the spark plug.  You could send 6 foot fire balls into the air. lol<BR>  <BR>   86se, I'm guessing your right.  Just wire in a coil just like the origonal one is and mount it close to the spark plug in the exhaust.  Then run a spark plug wire from the coil to the plug.  You'll need to install a switch in the power wire to the coil so you can turn it on and off.<P>  I'd be careful with this mod though.  The Fiero already ahd a bad enough reputation with fires.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000009||1FST2M6||07-27-2000||08:43 AM||||yes tap it into the stock coil wires just make sure the ground for the coil is broken with a switch. so you can shut it off!||||reg||1
Z||000010||b lo 0||07-27-2000||10:14 AM||||scarecrow, I think the thing about flames when you let off the gas in gear is the result of (possibly) valve overlap and compression braking.  Do you have a cam or anything?  It may also be that the stock cams have some degree of overlap.  If you ever watch touring cars or grand touring (a la Viper GTSR) when they go into a turn and let off the gas they spew all kinds of flames.  When the Vipers are in the pits you can actually see black marks behind the side pipes.  Just some thoughts.  Oh, yeah, rally cars do it too.<P>------------------<BR>'85 GT (in progress)  <BR>titled ICE-plates B LO 0 <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.angelfire.com/ga3/audioimagery/ice.gif">  <BR>Go to <A HREF="http://www.audioimagery.i-p.com" TARGET=_blank>www.audioimagery.i-p.com</A>  !!!||||reg||14
Z||000011||Standard||07-27-2000||11:27 AM||||Hmmm.. my car has no cat.. wonder if I'm gettin' any flames.. sure does make some cool popping noises when I let off the throttle. hehe<P>------------------<BR>Mike -- Golden Valley, MN<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 148,000 miles and counting!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000012||86SE||07-28-2000||12:57 AM||||After I do this mod, a fire extingusher wouldent be a bad idea.......just in case.... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>It would be awesome to race someone, get in front of them right away and give it full throttle acceleration!!  I would LOVE to see the look on their face..........<P>------------------<BR>'86 Special Edition,<BR>High-Output V-6 Yellow Fiero||||reg||10
